# SKIMA LPG — SAFE LOCATION & MAP PROVIDER MIGRATION TO LOCATIONIQ

# DO NOT DELETE THESE FILE


Continue the existing SKIMA LPG production application.

This task is a **full-stack location-runtime upgrade**.

This is NOT permission to rewrite the existing location system.

This is NOT permission to delete Google Maps.

This is NOT permission to delete Mapbox.

This is NOT permission to remove existing location screens, hooks, services, database tables, service-area logic, tracking logic, saved locations, coordinates, map components, permissions, or provider integrations.

The current location implementation represents substantial previous work.

## NON-NEGOTIABLE FIRST RULE

Before changing ANY location-related code:

**AUDIT THE ENTIRE CURRENT LOCATION IMPLEMENTATION.**

Do not modify files first.

Do not assume the existing implementation is wrong.

Do not replace existing architecture merely because a new provider is being introduced.

The objective is:

```text
EXISTING LOCATION SYSTEM
        ↓
Carefully audit and understand
        ↓
Preserve Google Maps implementation
        ↓
Preserve Mapbox implementation
        ↓
Introduce provider abstraction if missing
        ↓
Add LocationIQ
        ↓
Make LocationIQ the ACTIVE provider
        ↓
Keep Google Maps + Mapbox INACTIVE but fully intact
```

We must be able to re-enable Google Maps or Mapbox in the future without rebuilding those integrations.

